          "settings": {
            "label": "Why lean mass matters",
            "popup_title": "Why Lean Mass Matters",
            "popup_text": "<p>Muscle is metabolically active tissue and a major site of glucose disposal. Losing it during weight loss lowers your daily energy burn and worsens the fat-to-muscle ratio — a pattern linked to insulin resistance. Preserving it is what makes weight loss stick.</p>"
          }
        },
        "info_2": {
          "type": "info_button",
          "settings": {
            "label": "What is fat mass",
            "popup_title": "Fat Mass vs. Weight",
            "popup_text": "<p>The scale weighs everything — fat, muscle, water. Fat mass (measured here by bioelectrical impedance) tells you what portion of your body is fat. Two people can lose the same weight and end up in very different metabolic places depending on how much of it was fat versus muscle.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["stat_1", "stat_2", "info_1", "info_2"],
      "settings": {
