          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["attr_muscle", "attr_regain"],
      "settings": {
        "anchor": "glp1",
        "title": "A note on GLP-1 medications",
        "show_image_mobile": true,
        "background_heading": "What the research shows",
        "background_text": "GLP-1 medications (semaglutide and similar) produce large weight loss — and body-composition research reports that in some trials, 40–60% of the weight lost is lean mass, not fat.⁵ In the STEP 1 extension, participants regained about two-thirds of lost weight within a year of stopping.⁶ Inositol is not a GLP-1 and its effects are far smaller — but in the trial above, its fat loss came with lean mass preserved or increased. Different tools for different situations; talk to your doctor about what's right for you.",
        "attributes_heading": "The Numbers"
      }
    },
